---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="Theming" description="Tokens, layers, color scheme and the public style contract.">
  <div class="docs-content">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Theming</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Colors, radius, shadows and typography are CSS custom properties. The visual style lives in
      <code>styles/nova</code>; the structure lives in <code>components</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Layers</h2>
    <p>
      The generated <code>index.css</code> declares the layer order. Keep it before your own layers
      so component styles can be overridden deliberately.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`@layer loseta.tokens, loseta.reset, loseta.base, loseta.components, loseta.style, loseta.utilities;`}
    />

    <h2>Tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Tokens use the same names as shadcn/ui: <code>--background</code>, <code>--foreground</code>,
      <code>--primary</code>, <code>--muted</code>, <code>--border</code>, <code>--ring</code>,
      <code>--radius</code>, and so on.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`:root {
  --background: oklch(1 0 0);
  --foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  --primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
  --primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
  --border: oklch(0.922 0 0);
  --ring: oklch(0.708 0 0);
  --radius: 0.625rem;
}`}
    />

    <h2>Dark mode</h2>
    <p>
      Add <code>.dark</code> to the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element. The token file also sets
      <code>color-scheme</code> so native controls follow the color scheme.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="js" code={`document.documentElement.classList.toggle("dark", isDark);`} />

    <h2>Public style contract</h2>
    <p>
      Components expose variants, sizes and states through data attributes and ARIA. The most common
      hooks are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>data-variant</code> and <code>data-size</code> for visual variants.</li>
      <li><code>data-slot="title|description|action|header|shortcut|indicator"</code> for parts.</li>
      <li><code>aria-invalid="true"</code> for invalid controls.</li>
      <li><code>aria-selected="true"</code> for tabs, options and selectable rows.</li>
      <li><code>aria-checked="true"</code> for checkable menu items.</li>
      <li><code>data-highlighted</code> for the highlighted menu item.</li>
      <li><code>:disabled</code> and <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> for disabled states.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Styles</h2>
    <p>
      <code>styles/nova</code> is the default visual style. To create a new style, copy that folder,
      edit its files and point <code>loseta.json</code> at the new style when you initialize a
      project. v1 ships Nova only.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tokens are the primary customization surface. If a change cannot be expressed with tokens,
      edit the component or style file you own.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>No prefixes.</strong> Classes and tokens are intentionally unprefixed to match
      shadcn/ui and the source nomenclature. Use one design system per project to avoid collisions.
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
